=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  play engine/dns-udhcpc-alpine324 -----------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: engine/dns-udhcpc-alpine324$
# web-01.example.net runs Alpine 3.24; /etc/resolv.conf is a$
# file udhcpc writes on each lease, naming 192.0.2.1, and$
# udhcpc.conf is as installed. hardn.yml lists 192.0.2.54,$
# 2001:db8::54.$
# The change: Configure DNS, hardn.yml's nameservers. First$
# "Stop udhcpc rewriting /etc/resolv.conf?": y stops it in the$
# same change. Then y applies it; n declines.$
$
  Stop udhcpc rewriting /etc/resolv.conf? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
   -  Set nameservers; stop udhcpc rewriting$
      /etc/udhcpc/udhcpc.conf, /etc/resolv.conf$
      --- /etc/udhcpc/udhcpc.conf$
      +++ /etc/udhcpc/udhcpc.conf$
      @@ -2,3 +2,5 @@$
       #RESOLV_CONF="no"$
$
       #NO_DNS="eth1 wlan1"$
      +# hardn: keep udhcpc from rewriting /etc/resolv.conf$
      +RESOLV_CONF="no"$
      --- /etc/resolv.conf$
      +++ /etc/resolv.conf$
      @@ -1,2 +1,3 @@$
       search example.net$
      -nameserver 192.0.2.1$
      +nameserver 192.0.2.54$
      +nameserver 2001:db8::54$
$
  Configure DNS? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Set nameservers; stop udhcpc rewriting  Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
  Backup of /etc/udhcpc/udhcpc.conf, /etc/resolv.conf kept in$
  /var/backups/hardn/20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
$
  simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Info: engine/dns-udhcpc-alpine324$
# Recorded by the fake, not done: what each step ran on$
# web-01.example.net, and the files it changed, in order;$
# hardn's own journal, run directory and backups left out.$
$
   -  Applied: Set nameservers; stop udhcpc rewriting$
      /etc/udhcpc/udhcpc.conf, /etc/resolv.conf$
$

